  "body": "## What changed\n\nExterior contour rings that the user picks keep every requested depth when the complete cutter-center ring clears the model's XY convex hull.\nThe sign plate reaches Z 0 and keeps its four tabs.\nPicked contours refuse generation when a required deeper section cannot be read.\nThe error names the section failure and the skipped levels.\n\nThe hull proof applies only to picked rings (`contour_on_picked`, through `ladder_picked`).\nThe whole-model contour and the unpicked region contour keep the plain `ladder`.\nA whole-model contour on a broken mesh must refuse when a section cannot be read.\nThe hull proof skips each section, so it must not hide that refusal.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe depth ladder read interior sections even for a cutter outside the complete model footprint.\nA failed section could become a false floor.\nThe picked-ring check accepted this partial path after an earlier level succeeded.\n\n## Tests\n\nFinal head: 813e6a8cc. Base: `upstream/main` at 6e641dac7.\n\nPins:\n\n- `outside_sign_plate_reaches_bottom_with_four_tabs` (motion `contour_outside_floor`) checks every requested depth and four bottom cut runs.\n- `picked_ring_refuses_unread_deeper_plane_after_clear_levels` (motion `contour_outside_floor`) checks refusal after earlier levels succeed.\n- `whole_model_contour_that_cannot_reach_bottom_is_refused_with_the_stopped_level` (app `contour_whole_step`, unchanged) checks that a whole-model contour on a broken mesh refuses.\n\nPin proof:\n\n- The first two pins fail when the original `upstream/main` depth code is restored. The plate pin reports floor Z 7.061. The unread-section pin returns a partial path.\n- The third pin fails when the hull proof is put back into the shared `ladder`. It reports `deepest=-0.5`, the same failure that the review found. It passes when the fix is restored.\n\nCommands on the final head:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 146 steps, 0 failed.\n- All 13 app suites whose name starts with `contour`: all pass. `contour_whole_step`: 3 passed.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-motion --test contour_outside_floor`: 2 passed.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test example_catalog`: 37 passed, 4 ignored.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\nGate map gap: the quick gate does not select app `contour_whole_step` for this diff. The suite imports only `camcraft_app` re-exports, so the map does not link it to `motion::machining2d`.\n\nThe mesh fixture contains only the `sign` entity's saved triangles from the [reported q04 project](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/qa-artifacts/qa/round2-20261122/q04-vcarve-sign/q04-vcarve-sign-posted-5ops.camproj).\nThe test does not import STEP or load the saved toolpath.\n\n## Heavy lanes\n\n`cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main` ran on head 813e6a8cc19ab8598b648ec9f5c4cacc8db5d61e.\nThe base was `upstream/main` at 6e641dac753020bfed49fec310237eed28448141.\nThe diff reaches the `motion heavy` and `app heavy` lanes.\nResult: green. 244 steps ran, 0 failed. Wall time was 40.3 min.\nKnown-fail markers from main were red as expected (#1950, #2849).\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. `example_catalog` ran green on the final head.\nNo `.nc` or `.cl` files change.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe reported project was not run through the GUI or MCP.\nThe complete post flow for this project was not run.\nThe regression calls the motion generator on the saved model mesh.\nThe 0.02 mm allowance, `tab_count: 0`, and bottom-chain variants were not run separately.\n`contour_depth.rs` is 436 lines. It was 421 lines before this round, over the 400-line rule. This round adds the `ladder_in` seam. The picked wrapper is in `contour_exterior.rs`.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: Keep proven-clear picked outside contours at every requested depth and refuse unreadable partial picked contours.\n\nFixes #3443\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
